name: tightened-law
kind: inferred
shape: categorical
face: in
membrane: false
note: a surface the grammar admitted was found to declare something no
  consumer reads — accepted text whose declared semantics are silently
  dropped or miscompiled. Fires when the diff adds a refusal at the point
  the lie enters the AST (e.g. a default on a payload field the emitted
  union drops), closing a gap where no prior check stood. Sibling of
  widened-law: that one extends an existing check to new carriers; this
  one raises a new wall where the surface was never guarded.
